UID:10006607-1781956800-1781971200@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:A Day of Music & Art
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a vibrant Day of Art + Music with Decoda and artists from the Decoda Chamber Music Festival (DCMF). This all-ages experience invites you to explore the museum through sound\, creativity\, and connection.  \nEnjoy an interactive performance with Decoda artists\, take part in hands-on workshops that blend listening\, composing\, and visual art-making\, and wander the galleries on a self-guided musical tour—where works of art are paired with live performances by DCMF musicians. The day culminates in Arboretum in the Museum\, an immersive musical experience in which solo performances unfold simultaneously throughout the space\, transforming the museum into a living\, breathing soundscape. \nSchedule \nNoon–12:30pm — Live Music on the Plaza \n12:30–1:15pm — Interactive Performance in the Atrium (Decoda Artists) \n1:30–2pm — Workshop: Creative Art Making to Live Music in the Studio & Live Music on the Plaza \n2–2:45pm — Musical Gallery Tour in the Galleries \n2:45–3:15pm — Workshop: Creative Art Making to Live Music in the Studio \n3:30pm — Arboretum in the Museum by Decoda Bassoonist Brad Balliett.  A unique musical work featuring a collection of solos and duets inspired by different tree species. \n————— \nDecoda is an artist-led chamber music collective dedicated to creating a more compassionate and connected world through music. As Carnegie Hall’s only affiliate ensemble\, Decoda pairs virtuosic performance with deep community engagement\, bringing chamber music to concert halls\, schools\, shelters\, hospitals\, and correctional facilities. \nEach summer in the Asheville region\, Decoda leads the Decoda Chamber Music Festival\, a dynamic training program for young musicians who seek to develop both artistic excellence and social impact. Through side-by-side performances\, mentorship\, and creative collaboration\, participants explore how music can build community and inspire change. \nFree with Admission RESERVE TICKETS NOW
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/a-day-of-music-art/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/1DECODA_Titilayo-Ayangade-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
