UID:10006646-1783900800-1783987199@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Appalachian Arts & Crafts (Rising 9th - 12th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nBlending creativity with cultural heritage\, students will explore the artistic traditions of Appalachian culture through a series of hands-on crafts. They will begin the week creating vibrant painted barn quilts and learning basic weaving techniques with natural materials. They’ll spend the remainder of the week further developing their weaving skills to make reed baskets and needle felting a landscape.   \nMeet the Instructor: Kati Robbins\nKati Robbins has over 12 years of experience as an art educator\, teaching studio arts and crafts to a wide range of age groups in different learning environments. She is currently based in Asheville where she works as a high school art teacher. Her creative work focuses on mixed media and assemblage\, with a strong interest in collaborative and community based projects. She is inspired by Appalachian craft traditions\, natural materials and the surrounding landscape. When Kati isn’t teaching or making art\, she enjoys gardening\, cooking\, reading and hiking in the mountains. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-appalachian-arts-crafts/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/1976.62.71_New-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTSTAMP:20260620T002108
CREATED:20260127T210245Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182405Z
UID:10006651-1783900800-1783987199@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Exploring Photography Without a Camera (Rising 9th – 12th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nPhotography doesn’t always require a camera. In this experimental image lab\, students will explore photography-based processes that use light\, chemistry\, and transfer techniques to create images. Through hands-on exploration of cyanotypes\, lumen prints\, pinhole photography\, and image transfers\, students will experiment with transparency\, layering\, and transformation—creating works that blur the line between photography\, printmaking\, and mixed media.     \nMeet the Instructor: Kristina Shriver\nKristina Shriver is a visual art educator with over 16 years of experience\, working with students of all ages. She teaches at Asheville High School and serves as an AP Studio Art Reader and mentor for other art educators. Kristina designs hands-on\, material-rich art experiences that connect historical techniques to contemporary practice\, emphasizing experimentation\, personal storytelling\, and meaningful creative exploration. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-exploring-photography-without-a-camera-rising-9th-12th-grade/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/SC2011.01.96.jpg
END:VEVENT
